WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.160
Speaker 1: The American right wing has a number&nbsp;
of bogeymen, but one that has withstood the test&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.160 --> 00:00:09.600
of time is the IRS, which is why many on&nbsp;
the right right now are going apoplectic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:16.880
over the Biden administration's plan to hire&nbsp;
87,000 new IRS agents with the $80 billion that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.880 --> 00:00:22.480
they're getting from the Inflation Reduction Act&nbsp;
as a way to beef up tax enforcement and ultimately&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.480 --> 00:00:27.920
increase revenue for the federal government. So&nbsp;
the right they're trying to tie in the FBI raid of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:33.440
Donald Trump's home with the hiring of these IRS&nbsp;
agents, as if the two things have anything to do&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:38.720
with one another. I already showed you a clip of&nbsp;
Tulsi Gabbard trying to connect these dots earlier&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.720 --> 00:00:44.320
in the program, but she's not the only one. We&nbsp;
also have Florida Senator Marco Rubio who asked&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.320 --> 00:00:48.320
after today's raid on Mar a Lago, what&nbsp;
do you think the left plans to use those&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.040 --> 00:00:54.560
87,000 new agents for Rick Grenell, a former&nbsp;
Trump administration official tweeted, quote,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.560 --> 00:01:00.960
The FBI raids Trump's house and the Democrats&nbsp;
votes who had 87,000 new IRS agents to go after&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:07.600
Americans. Wake up, America. And then we have&nbsp;
Indiana Congressman Jim Banks, who said if the FBI&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:14.800
can raid the home of a former president, imagine&nbsp;
what 87,000 more IRS agents will do to you. Well,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.800 --> 00:01:20.400
the only connection that I can see between these&nbsp;
two things is that they involve agencies at the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:25.200
federal government under the executive branch.&nbsp;
But aside from that, it seems pretty weird to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:30.560
lump these two things together unless you want&nbsp;
to fearmonger and not care about the facts.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.120 --> 00:01:35.342
But then the rhetoric starts to get dangerous.&nbsp;
Because when you hear from some of these right&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.342 --> 00:01:39.760
wing personalities, they're trying to talk about&nbsp;
how the Biden administration wants to not only&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.760 --> 00:01:45.840
add to the IRS force, they also want to give&nbsp;
them new weapons. Brian KILMEADE, for example,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.840 --> 00:01:51.440
suggested on Fox News last week that these&nbsp;
new IRS agents are ready to hunt down&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.440 --> 00:01:56.880
and kill middle class taxpayers with the weapons&nbsp;
that they have. Let's take a look at the video.&nbsp;

00:01:56.880 --> 00:02:02.080
Speaker 3: The so-called Inflation Reduction&nbsp;
Act also says that $80 billion budget is for,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.080 --> 00:02:06.640
quote, increased enforcement, operational&nbsp;
improvements and customer service. What&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.640 --> 00:02:11.040
kind of customer service? We don't have to&nbsp;
wonder before the IRS took it down yesterday.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.040 --> 00:02:15.680
There was a posting. Watch this on their website.&nbsp;
They listed the job requirements for a special&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.680 --> 00:02:21.040
agents position. The major duties require agents&nbsp;
to, quote, carry a firearm and be willing to use&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:26.320
deadly force if necessary. A little like James&nbsp;
Bond. But instead of hunting down evil maniacs,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.320 --> 00:02:32.080
these agents hunt down and kill middle class&nbsp;
taxpayers that don't pay enough. It's Joe Biden's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.080 --> 00:02:36.880
new army. Americans are rightly concerned about&nbsp;
this. Got a new poll I'll share with you. Shows&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.880 --> 00:02:42.000
45% of the country fears the IRS will increase&nbsp;
the number of audits. According to the CNBC,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:46.640
which is another business network. The second&nbsp;
best financial experts are predicting the bill&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.640 --> 00:02:50.800
will spark more audits for small business owners.
Speaker 1: So what Brian KILMEADE was referring&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.800 --> 00:02:56.240
to in this clip is the IRS Criminal Investigation&nbsp;
Division, which is nothing new. It's been around&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.240 --> 00:03:00.880
for over a hundred years. They've always had&nbsp;
firearms training, and it's because they go&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.880 --> 00:03:05.440
after things like money laundering schemes and&nbsp;
cybercrime and situations that could get violent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.440 --> 00:03:11.200
or deadly. And so it makes sense for those agents&nbsp;
to be armed. But the average IRS auditor, when&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.200 --> 00:03:16.880
undergoing a routine audit, if someone is unarmed,&nbsp;
no surprise there. We also had Iowa Senator Chuck&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.880 --> 00:03:21.600
Grassley making this very same point that KILMEADE&nbsp;
made. He went on Fox and Friends and said, quote,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.600 --> 00:03:26.240
Are they going to have a strike force that&nbsp;
goes in with AK fifteens, already loaded,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.240 --> 00:03:31.120
ready to shoot some small business person&nbsp;
in Iowa? So first of all, he said AK 15,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:31.120 --> 00:03:36.800
which I thought wasn't a gun. I thought he&nbsp;
was mixing up a AR 15, an AK 47. He may have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.800 --> 00:03:40.960
mixed them up, but luckily he gets a pass&nbsp;
because it is a gun that exists, although&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.960 --> 00:03:44.960
it's quite rare. But if he was a Democrat and the&nbsp;
gun didn't exist, you better believe he would be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:44.960 --> 00:03:49.600
raked over the coals for making a statement like&nbsp;
that and not having an understanding of firearms.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:49.600 --> 00:03:55.200
But he just barely passed the test there. But the&nbsp;
broader point to his question is that, no, he's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.200 --> 00:03:59.680
just trying to feed into a conspiracy theory as to&nbsp;
what the Biden administration wants to accomplish&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.680 --> 00:04:04.400
by hiring all these agents and acting like it's&nbsp;
something nefarious or out of the ordinary.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.400 --> 00:04:10.400
But also the very idea that these agents are&nbsp;
going to go after people who make $50,000 a year,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.400 --> 00:04:15.600
60, $70,000 a year. It doesn't make a whole lot of&nbsp;
sense because, first of all, they've already said&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:15.600 --> 00:04:20.720
and it's been outlined in the text, you can look&nbsp;
at it. They're only going to look after look for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:20.720 --> 00:04:25.360
trying to recover money from people who make&nbsp;
$400,000 a year or more. But if you don't take&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:25.360 --> 00:04:30.160
them at their word, just think about it logically.&nbsp;
Just look at the math of the situation. So does it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:30.160 --> 00:04:35.680
make sense as an agency when you have limited&nbsp;
time, money, resources to go after Joe Schmo,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:35.680 --> 00:04:40.160
who makes 50 K a year with the hopes of maybe&nbsp;
recovering an extra couple of hundred dollars or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:40.160 --> 00:04:46.160
$1,000? Or does it make sense to put that time&nbsp;
and energy into scrutinizing someone who makes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:46.160 --> 00:04:51.520
$10 million a year or more with the idea that&nbsp;
maybe you can recover another million dollars,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:51.520 --> 00:04:55.600
couple of million dollars. Obviously, it&nbsp;
makes sense to investigate the wealthy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:55.600 --> 00:05:01.520
and also more revenue for the government means&nbsp;
that. We're going to be able to lower our debt and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:01.520 --> 00:05:06.880
deficit. All else being equal, I thought that the&nbsp;
right wing was in support of that. But of course,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:06.880 --> 00:05:11.120
we know that debt and deficit, they're a political&nbsp;
football, which at this point it's just not all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:11.120 --> 00:05:16.560
that convenient for Republicans to play with.&nbsp;
So they'll put that issue aside for now. So on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:16.560 --> 00:05:21.120
multiple fronts, the right wing fearmongering&nbsp;
about these new IRS agents doesn't make a whole&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:21.120 --> 00:05:26.320
lot of sense. But it's the perfect opportunity&nbsp;
